- How to test registry behavior and ensure isolation?
- What security considerations arise with remote or third-party validators?
- How to measure performance with many validators per field?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to extend behavior without touching core code, a common beginner design task. It also covers decoupling, simple registries, and safe runtime extension.

## Key Concepts
- Strategy pattern
- Registry / plugin registry
- Decoupling of validation logic from ingestion
- Runtime extensibility

## Code Example
```javascript
class Validator {
  validate(value) { throw new Error('not implemented') }
}

const registry = new Map<string, () => Validator>()

function register(field, factory) { registry.set(field, factory) }

function validate(field, value) {
  const factory = registry.get(field)
  if (!factory) throw new Error('no validator')
  return factory().validate(value)
}
```

